    {
      "id": "v02I7XBIx1wSCXtjiaol6",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5697.105285744537,
      "y": 2903.328588048493,
      "width": 659.95947265625,
      "height": 350,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1K",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 415172801,
      "version": 62,
      "versionNonce": 277004449,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1790351245828,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "from dataclasses import dataclass\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass Session:\n    id: str\n\n# Local session loader requires NO arguments\ndef get_local_session_client() -> Session:\n    return Session(id=\"local-static-token\")\n\n# API session loader requires explicit arguments\ndef get_api_session(api_client: HttpClient, user_id: str) -> Session:\n    response = api_client.get(f\"/users/{user_id}/session\")\n    return Session(token=response[\"token\"])",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "from dataclasses import dataclass\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass Session:\n    id: str\n\n# Local session loader requires NO arguments\ndef get_local_session_client() -> Session:\n    return Session(id=\"local-static-token\")\n\n# API session loader requires explicit arguments\ndef get_api_session(api_client: HttpClient, user_id: str) -> Session:\n    response = api_client.get(f\"/users/{user_id}/session\")\n    return Session(token=response[\"token\"])",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "I5kkRqRYARAgQ5_Q5REmw",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6625.193571360207,
      "y": 2827.4575902902366,
      "width": 1994.7984619140625,
      "height": 1950,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1L",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 98064047,
      "version": 6,
      "versionNonce": 1529051055,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1790352153510,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. PostgreSQL Schema & RLS Setup\nFirst, enable RLS on the sessions table and create a policy that checks a custom session variable (app.current_user_id).\n\nSQL\n-- 1. Create the sessions table\nCREATE TABLE sessions (\n    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n    user_id TEXT NOT NULL,\n    token TEXT NOT NULL,\n    created_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT NOW()\n);\n\n-- 2. Enable Row-Level Security\nALTER TABLE sessions ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;\n\n-- 3. Create isolation policy\n-- Note: 'app.current_user_id' is a custom session variable set dynamically per request/connection\nCREATE POLICY user_session_isolation_policy ON sessions\n    FOR ALL\n    USING (user_id = current_setting('app.current_user_id', true));\n2. Python & SQLAlchemy Implementation\nIn SQLAlchemy, you execute SET LOCAL app.current_user_id = ... immediately after opening a database session/transaction. SET LOCAL ensures the variable is scoped strictly to the current transaction.\n\nPython\nfrom contextlib import contextmanager\nfrom typing import Generator\nfrom sqlalchemy import Column, String, DateTime, create_engine, text\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import DeclarativeBase, Session, sessionmaker\n\nDATABASE_URL = \"postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/mydatabase\"\n\nengine = create_engine(DATABASE_URL, echo=False)\nSessionFactory = sessionmaker(bind=engine)\n\n# ORM Model\nclass Base(DeclarativeBase):\n    pass\n\nclass UserSession(Base):\n    __tablename__ = \"sessions\"\n\n    id = Column(String, primary_key=True)\n    user_id = Column(String, nullable=False)\n    token = Column(String, nullable=False)\n\n# Helper context manager for user-scoped DB sessions\n@contextmanager\ndef scoped_session(user_id: str) -> Generator[Session, None, None]:\n    \"\"\"Yields a database session restricted strictly to the given user_id.\"\"\"\n    session = SessionFactory()\n    try:\n        # Set the PostgreSQL session variable for the current transaction\n        session.execute(\n            text(\"SELECT set_config('app.current_user_id', :user_id, true)\"),\n            {\"user_id\": user_id}\n        )\n        yield session\n        session.commit()\n    except Exception:\n        session.rollback()\n        raise\n    finally:\n        session.close()\n3. Usage Example\nNotice that the ORM query does not include any WHERE user_id = ... clause. PostgreSQL handles the isolation automatically behind the scenes.\n\nPython\n# --- User 1 Context ---\nwith scoped_session(user_id=\"user_abc\") as db:\n    # Query all sessions — Postgres automatically filters to 'user_abc'\n    sessions = db.query(UserSession).all()\n    print(\"User ABC sees sessions:\", [s.token for s in sessions])\n\n# --- User 2 Context ---\nwith scoped_session(user_id=\"user_xyz\") as db:\n    # Query all sessions — Postgres automatically filters to 'user_xyz'\n    sessions = db.query(UserSession).all()\n    print(\"User XYZ sees sessions:\", [s.token for s in sessions])",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. PostgreSQL Schema & RLS Setup\nFirst, enable RLS on the sessions table and create a policy that checks a custom session variable (app.current_user_id).\n\nSQL\n-- 1. Create the sessions table\nCREATE TABLE sessions (\n    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n    user_id TEXT NOT NULL,\n    token TEXT NOT NULL,\n    created_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT NOW()\n);\n\n-- 2. Enable Row-Level Security\nALTER TABLE sessions ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;\n\n-- 3. Create isolation policy\n-- Note: 'app.current_user_id' is a custom session variable set dynamically per request/connection\nCREATE POLICY user_session_isolation_policy ON sessions\n    FOR ALL\n    USING (user_id = current_setting('app.current_user_id', true));\n2. Python & SQLAlchemy Implementation\nIn SQLAlchemy, you execute SET LOCAL app.current_user_id = ... immediately after opening a database session/transaction. SET LOCAL ensures the variable is scoped strictly to the current transaction.\n\nPython\nfrom contextlib import contextmanager\nfrom typing import Generator\nfrom sqlalchemy import Column, String, DateTime, create_engine, text\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import DeclarativeBase, Session, sessionmaker\n\nDATABASE_URL = \"postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/mydatabase\"\n\nengine = create_engine(DATABASE_URL, echo=False)\nSessionFactory = sessionmaker(bind=engine)\n\n# ORM Model\nclass Base(DeclarativeBase):\n    pass\n\nclass UserSession(Base):\n    __tablename__ = \"sessions\"\n\n    id = Column(String, primary_key=True)\n    user_id = Column(String, nullable=False)\n    token = Column(String, nullable=False)\n\n# Helper context manager for user-scoped DB sessions\n@contextmanager\ndef scoped_session(user_id: str) -> Generator[Session, None, None]:\n    \"\"\"Yields a database session restricted strictly to the given user_id.\"\"\"\n    session = SessionFactory()\n    try:\n        # Set the PostgreSQL session variable for the current transaction\n        session.execute(\n            text(\"SELECT set_config('app.current_user_id', :user_id, true)\"),\n            {\"user_id\": user_id}\n        )\n        yield session\n        session.commit()\n    except Exception:\n        session.rollback()\n        raise\n    finally:\n        session.close()\n3. Usage Example\nNotice that the ORM query does not include any WHERE user_id = ... clause. PostgreSQL handles the isolation automatically behind the scenes.\n\nPython\n# --- User 1 Context ---\nwith scoped_session(user_id=\"user_abc\") as db:\n    # Query all sessions — Postgres automatically filters to 'user_abc'\n    sessions = db.query(UserSession).all()\n    print(\"User ABC sees sessions:\", [s.token for s in sessions])\n\n# --- User 2 Context ---\nwith scoped_session(user_id=\"user_xyz\") as db:\n    # Query all sessions — Postgres automatically filters to 'user_xyz'\n    sessions = db.query(UserSession).all()\n    print(\"User XYZ sees sessions:\", [s.token for s in sessions])",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
